WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.680
Glad to have you with us on Tesla's short time, episode 552, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.560
It's July 25th, 2026.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.920
Lots happening across deliveries, FSD, and the stock today.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:21.240
Tesla's FSD V14.3.6 now pulls into Sheet's entrances and assigned home spots that previously

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.680
needed manual driving.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:29.060
Tesla reported revenue growth in its latest quarter alongside continued pressure on automotive

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:29.660
margins.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:36.720
Spending on AI, Robotaxi, and Optimus programs contributed to that margin compression during

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.380
the period.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:43.680
Energy storage and software services delivered record-profit contributions that helped offset

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.940
weaker vehicle results.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.200
Investors are weighing the balance between near-term profitability and the longer-term autonomy

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:51.740
investments.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.740
This financial picture connects directly to how autonomy software is advancing in practice.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:06.000
The latest FSD V14.3.6 update lets the car enter a local Sheet's driveway that earlier

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.700
versions had never handled, despite repeated manual use of the same entrance.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.880
It also parks in the owner's assigned home space even when other spots remain open.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:22.060
These changes address specific real-world navigation gaps that have persisted across earlier

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:22.640
versions.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.760
The improvements come as Tesla continues iterating on supervised FSD ahead of any unsupervised

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.060
regulatory path.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:37.620
From passenger vehicle FSD progress, the focus now shifts to plans for commercial trucks.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:43.740
Elon Musk stated that FSD capability will reach the semi by early 2027.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:49.980
The timeline aligns with broader efforts to expand supervised autonomy across Tesla's commercial

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:50.880
vehicle lineup.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:56.540
No details were given on regulatory approval or specific semi-production volumes.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:02.380
The semi-program continues limited customer deployments while production scaling remains

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:02.980
gradual.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.360
From vehicle autonomy, the next major hardware program involves optimists.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:13.980
Tesla is sourcing components for optimists from Chinese suppliers as it prepares for higher

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.960
volume production.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:21.040
Elon Musk stated that supply chain constraints remain the primary obstacle to scaling.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:27.320
The move follows ongoing factory construction at Giga, Texas, where dedicated optimist lines

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:28.200
are being built.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:33.440
Volume targets stay pin to 2027 and beyond under current plans.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.100
From new product programs, an existing production challenge involves cyber truck tooling.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:45.280
Tesla filed suit claiming a Texas supplier is withholding custom tooling and parts unless

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.940
paid $250,000 per day.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.740
The company states it owns the tooling outright and needs it returned to maintain cyber truck

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.640
production flow.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.800
The emergency order request focuses on reclaiming property rather than resolving payment disputes.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.260
Production at Giga, Texas, remains exposed while the legal process continues.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:12.540
Owning the physical tooling for a component changes the balance of power in any supplier dispute.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.180
When a manufacturer controls the dies, molds, and fixtures required to make a part,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:22.700
it can shift production or bring work in-house without starting from scratch.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.860
Tesla's lawsuit over the cyber truck supplier illustrates this leverage in practice because

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:34.720
the company is not arguing price or quality, but simply demanding return of assets it already

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.400
paid to create. The result is faster legal resolution than a typical contract fight and

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:46.360
lower risk of prolonged line stoppage. This approach carries its own costs because designing and

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:52.040
building custom tooling requires upfront capital and engineering time that many automakers preferred

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:58.100
outsource. Tesla accepts that burden because it aligns with a broader pattern of controlling the

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:04.100
variables that most affect production velocity. In a high mix environment that now includes

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:10.720
vehicles, energy products, and humanoid robots, the ability to redirect tooling quickly becomes a

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:16.920
competitive advantage rather than a sunk cost. The downstream effect appears in margin protection

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.680
because supply interruptions measured in days instead of weeks help avoid both lost revenue and

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:29.040
the secondary costs of expedited freight or temporary workarounds. From one cyber truck production

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:35.780
issue, the next development involves energy product compatibility. Existing Powerwall 2 installations

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:41.600
in Australia can now accept a Powerwall 3 unit without additional gateway or inverter hardware.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:48.340
The upgrade path simplifies capacity expansion for Australian households already using the earlier

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:54.640
model. This change reduces installation cost and complexity for owners seeking more storage.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:01.580
Tesla has not detailed whether similar compatibility will reach other markets. From energy product

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:06.340
compatibility, reported reliability issues have surfaced with the newer unit.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:12.680
Owners report the Powerwall 3 halts charging following even brief grid interruptions and the

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:19.260
mobile app fails to display any grid flow data. This behavior leaves the system unable to resume normal

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:25.980
operation without intervention. The issue surfaces in residential energy storage where reliable post

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:32.380
outage recovery matters most. Tesla has not yet issued a software fix or statement on the reported

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:39.000
behavior. From energy hardware, a regulatory note on vehicle design closes out the vehicle side.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:45.140
The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration rejected a petition calling for a formal probe

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:51.660
into interior door release mechanisms on Tesla vehicles. The agency stated it found insufficient

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:57.760
evidence to warrant further action at this time. The decision follows earlier reports of incidents

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:03.620
involving the electronic door handles. Tesla maintains the current design meets all applicable

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:09.820
safety standards. From regulatory clearance, a supply chain positive rounds out the manufacturing

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:17.860
updates. LG Energy Solution will deliver battery cells valued at $4.3 billion under a new multi-year

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:23.440
agreement. The supply supports Tesla's vehicle production across multiple platforms including

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:30.260
Model Y and Cybertruck. This contract adds to Tesla's existing cell sourcing from multiple suppliers.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.660
No specific cell chemistry or factory allocation details were released. Edmunds published the

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:43.980
full pricing breakdown for the refreshed 2026 Model Y across all trims. The details show how Tesla

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:50.300
positioned the updated vehicle relative to prior model year pricing. Buyers now have clearer line

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:56.360
item comparisons for range, performance, and feature differences. The release comes as Tesla

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:02.700
continues to adjust its core vehicle lineup amid competitive pressure. Auto Express compared the

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:09.880
Tesla Model 3 directly against Mazda's new 6E electric sedan on range, handling, and interior space.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:16.780
The test highlights how Mazda's first dedicated EV stacks up against an established benchmark in

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:22.900
the segment. Real-world driving impressions and charging performance form the core of the evaluation.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:28.740
The match-up arrives as more traditional automakers enter the compact EV space.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:35.240
A comparison tracked fuel, maintenance, and energy costs over equivalent distances for a hydrogen

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:42.840
Toyota Mirai and a Tesla Model Y. The Tesla Model Y showed lower operating expenses primarily due

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:49.020
to electricity versus hydrogen pricing in the tested region. Real-world refueling times and

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:55.480
infrastructure access also factored into the final tally. The exercise underscores ongoing total

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:02.180
cost of ownership differences between battery and hydrogen powertrains. One article examines leasing

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:08.980
versus buying for Tesla vehicles amid rapid technology shifts. The piece outlines how leasing structures

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:14.460
shift residual value risk away from the buyer in a market with rapid technology changes.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:21.040
Buyers considering purchase face uncertainty around future software features and model refreshes.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:27.600
Leasing allows access to newer hardware and FSD updates without long-term ownership commitment.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:34.240
The piece notes this dynamic applies across Tesla's current lineup amid ongoing autonomy development.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:40.460
The discussion appears on motor1.com and focuses on current model year considerations.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.280
Source material comes from Google News aggregation of the motor1.com report.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:53.120
Video footage shows a Cybertruck unable to complete a boat launch on a ramp. The incident required

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:58.840
assistance from a conventional truck to finish the task. The event highlights real-world towing

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:05.740
limits under specific conditions such as incline and surface traction. Tesla has not commented on the video

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:11.620
or the circumstances shown. Cybertruck towing ratings remain published at the vehicle's maximum

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:18.540
specified capacity. The clip circulated via Yahoo Auto's coverage. There is a challenge worth

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:24.640
discussing around the Cybertruck supplier situation. Tesla claims a supplier is withholding

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:30.260
owned tooling and demanding daily payments to release it, directly threatening Cybertruck line

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:36.820
continuity at Gigatexus. The lawsuit seeks an emergency order to reclaim the property rather than

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:42.400
negotiate payment terms. Production exposure remains until the court resolves access.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:48.900
This situation tests how quickly Tesla can secure alternative sourcing or legal relief to protect

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:54.920
output targets. Before we go, keep an eye on any developments in the supplier tooling lawsuit

00:09:54.920 --> 00:10:01.560
and whether similar Powerwall 3 compatibility expands beyond Australia. That covers it for today's

